    feat: sweep-status --decide — machine-checkable decisions for off-vocab rows. Addresses REVIEW-BOARDCTL-001.
    
    Fleet census (2026-09-30, ~52 boards) showed every remaining off-vocabulary
    row is either a guard_result/ci_result carrying recoverable prose ("PASS 5/5",
    "PASS (secrets)", "pipeline 1166 SUCCESS all 6 jobs", "N/A (bash script; ...)")
    or a recycled-id status:"duplicate" row that dedupe-board --by-id refuses
    (the dedupe deadlock: sweep can't fix them, dedupe refuses them).
    
    --decide re-classifies exactly two classes by machine-checkable rules;
    everything else keeps refusing to guess:
    
    - result columns by CONTENT RULES: ambiguity gate first (a value naming both
      PASS and FAIL stays explicit, wherever the words sit), then first-token
      PASS|OK->PASS / FAIL|ERROR->FAIL / GREEN->GREEN / RED->RED, then standalone
      SKIP or literal N/A -> SKIP, then standalone SUCCESS -> GREEN (ci) /
      PASS (guard) and standalone OK -> PASS. PENDING is NEVER rewritten (the
      check has not run); ambiguous and unmatched values stay explicit.
    - status "duplicate" WITH an earlier same-id twin closes through the
      DF-BOARDCTL-10 path (new per-line Board.CloseIDDupeLine: status=complete,
      superseded_by, worker_summary naming the kept line, completed_at, one
      audit event quoting title/reasoning/pre-close status verbatim). A
      "duplicate" with NO earlier twin stays explicit. dedupe-board itself is
      untouched (option (b) of the design: sweep --decide handles duplicates).
    
    Writes (only under --decide --apply; --decide alone stays dry-run) go through
    two narrow sanctioned writers, both keeping the BT-007 vocabulary gate INTACT:
    - new Board.SetResultValue: the update --guard/--ci machinery reduced to one
      field — value must already be a canonical member of the named column's
      vocabulary, unknown ids/columns refuse, untouched lines byte-identical.
    - Board.CloseIDDupeLine: refusals for out-of-range/header/no-id/keep-side
      lines, nothing written on any refusal; per-row skip-and-report on failure,
      never a mid-file abort.
    
    Also in this change:
    - decide rows are reported on StatusSweepRow (Decided/DecidedValue/Reason +
      the dup plan: DupKeptLine/DupSupersede); the decision table is
      ResultDecideRuleDoc, printed by sweep-status --help and pinned by a
      doc-vs-function cross-check test.
    - help text + README section (follows the BT-066 sweep-status pattern) +
      usage text document the exact table.
    - legacy behavior unchanged WITHOUT --decide (pinned by a CLI test): prose
      rows stay explicit even under --apply; validate/read.go untouched.
    
    Tests: decision-table units (every census example + refusal arms),
    board-level decide dry-run/apply/idempotence, per-line close quoting
    status_was "duplicate", SetResultValue gate arms, CLI-level acceptance
    fixtures A-C and the no-decide regression.
    
    Battery: go build, go vet, go test -short ./..., make fmt-check,
    make version-check — all green. Write-path vocab enforcement unchanged
    (writers still reject off-vocab values; update LIVE-PENDING --ci MAYBE
    still exits 1).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
